.TH SENTINELRECON 1 "August 2026" "SentinelRecon v1.1.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
sentinelrecon \- Adaptive reconnaissance and vulnerability correlation engine
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sentinelrecon
[\fITARGET\fR] [\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.br
.B sentinelrecon
\fICOMMAND\fR [\fIARGS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
SentinelRecon is an adaptive reconnaissance and evidence correlation framework designed for authorized penetration testing, security audits, and laboratory assessments. It integrates network discovery, service capability classification (AJP, Web, SSH, SMB, DNS, Databases), web technology fingerprinting, autonomous content discovery, and evidence-based vulnerability intelligence into a unified pipeline.

.SH INTERACTIVE MODE
Running \fBsentinelrecon\fR without arguments launches the interactive mode, prompting for Target (IP or URL) and Recon Mode (1. Standard Recon or 2. Low-Impact Recon). Content discovery profiles are selected and composed autonomously based on detected services and technologies.

.SH TARGET USAGE
.B sentinelrecon <IP>
.br
.B sentinelrecon -u http://<TARGET>:<PORT>
.br
.B sentinelrecon -u https://<TARGET>:<PORT>
.br
.B sentinelrecon --url https://example.com

.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
.TP
.B --mode standard
STANDARD reconnaissance mode. Performs full discovery including service detection, default scripts, and technology fingerprinting.
.TP
.B --mode low-impact
LOW-IMPACT reconnaissance mode. Reduces request rates, respects Retry-After headers, and avoids duplicate requests.
.TP
.B --version
Displays the installed SentinelRecon version (v1.1.0).
.TP
.B -h, --help
Displays command-line help and usage information.

.SH OFFLINE ANALYSIS
.B sentinelrecon import <dir>
.br
Imports a directory of scan outputs and stores them in a session.
.br
.B sentinelrecon analyze <file>
.br
Analyzes a single scan output file and normalizes findings.

.SH SESSIONS AND REPORTS
.B sentinelrecon sessions
.br
Lists stored scan sessions.
.br
.B sentinelrecon show <session_id>
.br
Displays terminal summary for a specific session (use \fBcurrent\fR for the latest session).
.br
.B sentinelrecon report <session_id> [--format terminal|json|html] [--output <file>]
.br
Generates a report for a session in terminal, JSON, or HTML format.
.br
.B sentinelrecon waf <session_id>
.br
Displays WAF and CDN analysis for a session.

.SH CAPABILITY & PROVIDER STATUS
.B sentinelrecon tools
.br
Displays application capabilities and their underlying external provider status.

.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
sentinelrecon
sentinelrecon 10.49.128.206
sentinelrecon 10.10.10.25 --mode low-impact
sentinelrecon -u http://10.49.128.206:8080
sentinelrecon sessions
sentinelrecon show current
sentinelrecon report current --format html
sentinelrecon tools
.fi

.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 on error.
